abstract: >-
  This report defines memory as a computational concept distinct from storage,
  proposes a recall algebra closed over an explicit memory state, normal forms
  for well-formed traces, and twelve conformance rules for systems that claim
  to be memory engines. The model borrows tier physics, decay, and emotional
  modulation from cognitive science as named failure modes; it does not assert
  biological substrate identity.
